KZ3 patch 2035: texture content changes update the cached resource in place (RSX pass 35; RE pass 72 proposal 2).
A refresh (a bound texture whose content hash changed) decoded into a new committed resource, rewrote the SRV and
retired the old resource; in the level that is ~240 a frame, nearly all of them 8x8 fp16 textures rewritten every
frame. The refresh now offers the entry's resource to create_texture_mipped, which copies the new texels into it
when the description matches (PIXEL_SHADER_RESOURCE -> COPY_DEST -> PIXEL_SHADER_RESOURCE around the same upload
ring copies). LD_TEX_INPLACE=0 restores the old path; [tex-hash] gains inplace=N per 256 frames.
Upstream candidate (general: any title that rewrites small textures every frame).

--- a/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
@@ -2419,6 +2419,23 @@
 
 typedef struct { u32 w, h; const u8* data; u32 row_bytes, rows; } tex_level_t;
 
+/* KZ3 patch 2035: content changes update the cached resource in place. A refresh (the bound texture's hash
+ * changed) used to decode into a new committed resource, rewrite the SRV and retire the old one; in the KZ3 level
+ * that is ~240 per frame, nearly all 8x8 fp16 textures rewritten every frame (RE pass 72, proposal 2). With
+ * g_ld_tex_reuse set by the refresh path, create_texture_mipped copies the new texels into that resource when its
+ * description matches (2D, size, mip count, format): PIXEL_SHADER_RESOURCE -> COPY_DEST, the same upload-ring
+ * copies, back to PIXEL_SHADER_RESOURCE. Draws recorded earlier read the old texels (the barrier orders them before
+ * the copy), later draws the new ones, the same as a new resource gave. LD_TEX_INPLACE=0 restores the old path.
+ * Cube, 3D and vertex textures keep the old path. Counted in [tex-hash] as inplace=N. */
+static ID3D12Resource* g_ld_tex_reuse;
+static unsigned long long g_ld_tex_inplace_n;
+static int ld_tex_inplace_on(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) { const char* e = getenv("LD_TEX_INPLACE"); on = (e && e[0] == '0') ? 0 : 1; }
+    return on;
+}
